    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 47 tests pass, including `Cp34Tests` (the age-band acceptance test), with no regressions. **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` feature so the application fully satisfies the specification: when a request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the owner response returns `ageBand` as `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as the owner's age on the `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `birthDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `birth_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps `birthDate` from the request DTO into the entity.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", ...)` and an `ageBand(Owner)` method that computes the band via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`, returning `null` (so the field is omitted) when no `birthDate` is held.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `birth_date DATE` column to all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql). Updated the hsqldb `data.sql` positional owner inserts (the ones tests load under the `hsqldb` profile) with a trailing NULL; h2/postgres data use named-column inserts and needed no change.\n\nI chose a plain string for `ageBand` (rather than a generated enum) to stay consistent with the other derived string fields (`contactPreference`, `locality`) and to keep the MapStruct expression simple.",
